{
  "name": "Channel Divinity: Feat of Strength",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can use your Channel Divinity to enhance your physical might. When you fail an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw using Strength, you can use your Channel Divinity to gain a +10 bonus to the roll. Alternatively, when a creature within 30 feet of you fails an Attack Roll, Ability Check, or Saving Throw using Strength, you can use your Reaction to grant that creature a +10 bonus to the roll, using your Channel Divinity. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the roll succeeds or fail.</p>",
